  "term": "level of measurement",
  "definition": "Level of measurement refers to the kind of scale used to describe data. Common levels are nominal, which uses labels; ordinal, which ranks values without true quantitative spacing; interval, which has equal units but no true zero; and ratio, which has equal units and a true zero, allowing meaningful comparisons such as one value being twice another.",
